s one of the carriers involved in the ammonia ship-to-ship transfer operation with MOL", "MURALI SRINIVASAN:Murali Srinivasan is the senior vice president and commercial head at Yara, who commented on the significance of the ammonia ship-to-ship transfer operation", "AUSTRALIA:Australia is a country where the ammonia cargo transfer operation took place, specifically in the Pilbara region. Additionally, the region is experiencing port congestion, which is affecting vehicle exports.", "NOV 19:The date when Japan's Mitsui O.S.K. Lines and Kansai Electric Power Company signed a memorandum of understanding for the joint study of a liquefied hydrogen carrier", "OCT 23:The date when Singapore LNG Corporation agreed to charter a floating storage and regasification unit from Mitsui O.S.K. Lines", "SEPT 19:The date when Japan's Mitsui O.S.K. Lines, Norway's Yara, and Singapore's Global Centre for Maritime Decarbonisation completed an ammonia cargo transfer operation in Australia", "SINGAPORE:", "WILLIAM CLARK:William Clark is the contact person and Sales Director for Tesla, Inc. in the procurement agreement", "\"K\" LINE:\"K\" LINE, also known as Kawasaki Kisen Kaisha, Ltd., is a logistics company rooted in the shipping industry, operating a diverse fleet of more than 400 vessels worldwide. Established in 1919, it provides reliable maritime transport services and focuses on digital transformation, environmental technologies, and safety/ship quality management to offer safe and optimized services that prioritize the customer.\"", "INMARSAT MARITIME:Inmarsat Maritime, a Viasat company, powers the digitalization of the maritime industry with over 40 years of experience. It offers reliable and innovative solutions that enable ship owners and operators to stay connected, navigate safely, enhance operational efficiency, and ensure crew welfare. Inmarsat Maritime is based in Viasat’s global international business headquarters in London, United Kingdom.", "VIASAT:Viasat is a global communications company that believes everyone and everything in the world can be connected. With offices in 24 countries, Viasat is developing a global communications network to provide high-quality, reliable, secure, affordable, and fast connections. In May 2023, Viasat completed its acquisition of Inmarsat, combining the teams, technologies, and resources of the two companies to create a new global communications partner.", "NEXUSWAVE:NexusWave is a new bonded network service launched by Inmarsat Maritime in May 2023. It integrates multiple high-speed networks in real time to enable high-speed, always-on ship-to-shore communications. NexusWave offers high-speed connectivity, unlimited data, global coverage, and secure infrastructure for office-like and home-like experiences. It integrates Global Xpress (GX) Ka-band, low-Earth orbit (LEO) services, and coastal LTE service, enhanced by an L-band layer for resiliency."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}